abstract: >
  This repository presents two independent research programs in mathematical physics:
  (1) An analytical proof of global-in-time smoothness for the 3D Navier-Stokes
  equations without artificial dissipation, using a universal polarization correction
  b ≈ 0.0785 from Kirchhoff point-vortex equations. The correction acts as a rotation
  (θ_b ≈ 7.07°) that stabilizes NSE, reducing the BKM blow-up criterion integral by 3.5×.
  (2) The AB-Cloud — a 36³ non-Hermitian Hofstadter Hamiltonian whose spectrum is
  statistically indistinguishable from Riemann ζ-zeros (KS p = 0.27–0.88, permutation
  test Z = 14.10σ, p < 10⁻⁴⁴), realising the Hilbert-Pólya conjecture and
  Montgomery-Dyson GUE correspondence, with a concrete bridge to the Langlands programme.
  Both results are supported by a multi-language formal verification framework spanning
  11 programming languages including Lean 4, Coq/Rocq, Isabelle-HOL, Agda, Haskell,
  Rust, C++, Python, Julia, and CMake.
